VERSION 7: INFRASTRUCTURE AS CODE (IaC) & AWS CLOUD ARCHITECTURE (V7)
================================================================================

[GOAL]
Provision a highly available, secure, production-grade cloud infrastructure on 
Amazon Web Services (AWS) using Terraform (or AWS CDK) and deploy MiniCommerce to 
AWS ECS Fargate behind an Application Load Balancer.

[KEY DELIVERABLES & ARCHITECTURE]

1. Terraform Modular Infrastructure Layout (`terraform/`):
   - `modules/vpc`:
     * AWS VPC across 2 Availability Zones (AZs) in `us-east-1` (or `ap-south-1`).
     * 2 Public Subnets (for ALB & NAT Gateways).
     * 2 Private Application Subnets (for ECS Fargate backend/worker/frontend tasks).
     * 2 Private Database Subnets (for RDS PostgreSQL & ElastiCache Redis).
     * Internet Gateway + 2 NAT Gateways for secure outbound internet access from private subnets.
   - `modules/rds`:
     * AWS RDS PostgreSQL (Postgres 15) Multi-AZ instance in private database subnets.
     * DB Subnet Group, Security Groups restricting access exclusively from ECS security group.
     * Storage Encryption using AWS KMS (`aws_kms_key`).
     * Automated daily snapshots, backup retention (7 days), and `performance_insights_enabled`.
   - `modules/elasticache`:
     * AWS ElastiCache Redis Replication Group in private database subnets.
     * Transit Encryption (TLS) and At-Rest Encryption.
     * Redis AUTH token integration stored in AWS Secrets Manager.
   - `modules/ecs`:
     * AWS ECS Fargate Cluster (`minicommerce-cluster`).
     * ECS Task Definitions for `backend` (FastAPI), `worker` (ARQ), and `frontend` (Nginx).
     * ECS Service Definitions with target groups connected to Application Load Balancer (ALB).
     * Target Tracking Auto-Scaling Policies:
       - Scale OUT when average CPU utilization > 70% or Memory > 80%.
       - Scale IN when utilization normalizes.
   - `modules/alb`:
     * AWS Application Load Balancer in public subnets.
     * HTTP Listener (Port 80) automatically redirecting to HTTPS (Port 443).
     * HTTPS Listener with AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) SSL/TLS Certificate.
   - `modules/iam_and_secrets`:
     * IAM Task Execution Roles with least-privilege policies.
     * AWS Secrets Manager integration: FastAPI dynamically fetches `DATABASE_URL`, `REDIS_URL`, and `JWT_SECRET` at container startup via AWS SDK (`boto3`) or environment injection.

2. Environments Separation (`terraform/environments/`):
   - `environments/staging/` (`main.tf`, `variables.tf`, `terraform.tfvars`).
   - `environments/prod/` (`main.tf`, `variables.tf`, `terraform.tfvars`).
   - Remote State Storage: AWS S3 Bucket for Terraform state files + AWS DynamoDB table for state locking (`LockID`).

